  "notes": {
    "Q1": "The worker RNG is seeded by a bare srand with no argument. The return value is not stored. The worker startup line prints pid and hostname, not the seed.",
    "Q2": "The ordered suite list is the in-memory @suite_stats array, dumped to /tmp/test_queue_worker_<pid>_suites, then deleted by the master after it is loaded.",
    "Q3": "TEST_QUEUE_STATS defaults to .test_queue_stats. Each suite record is name, path, duration, and last_seen_at, stored in a hash keyed by name. No worker id or pid field.",
    "Q4": "Iterator#each yields each suite. Runner#after_fork_internal(num, iterator) runs in the forked worker and then calls after_fork(num). num is 1-based (i + 1).",
    "Q5": "QueueRunner is built from ARGV once. run_worker calls run_each and neither method assigns configuration.seed. The master prints configuration.seed. The worker inherits that configuration.",
    "C1": "parallel_tests groups files statically and reprints a failing group with command_with_seed, which appends --seed. The control tree has no srand call.",
    "O6": "An RSpec suite name is example_or_group.id when that method exists, otherwise full_description, otherwise metadata[:full_description], otherwise metadata[:example_group][:full_description]. split_groups keeps top-level groups, and yields each group's descendant examples when TEST_QUEUE_SPLIT_GROUPS=true, except groups whose metadata no_split is set.",
    "O7": "ExampleGroup.failure_count maps status == 'failed' and then takes length, so the integer equals the number of direct examples, failed or not. Iterator#each adds that integer to @failures. @failures is compared with @early_failure_limit in the same file. The inference that the limit misfires on a real run is UNPROVEN until Part B. This entry is a static observation only."
  },
